  "created": "2018-10-13T23:14:52.960Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The Desktop crouching has looked broken ever since the beta of the trust system to where it looked like it didn't use a crouching animation at all, but instead moved your idle down with the viewpoint or something like that. Then, when that update went live... it was still broken, but in a different way, it still looked like that, but the arms were out in the front, rigid, which looked really bad... Now, in the current beta, it looks exactly how it did in the trust system beta... even with a custom crouch animation. The prone looked broken from the start when it was added... in the trust update it got a little better, except for the rigid arms, but in the current beta, the arms are in the position like the one vr users get when they're prone and lose tracking. This could get very frustrating to people with models that have big sleeves/arms, and would look way better if the arms weren't in view. When desktop prone was first added, the way it looked to other people, and I don't understand why it didn't look that way in your point of view. The first two images are from the current beta, and the last image is from when desktop  crouching and prone were first added.",
